Instead of storing data randomly in files, a DBMS provides a structured and controlled way to manage data

A DBMS helps us:
- Store data
- Retrieve data quickly
- Update data safely
- Delete data when needed
- Prevent accidental loss
- Control access
- Support multiple users simultaneously

Think of a DBMS as a professional librarian
-> Without a librarian, finding a single book would take hours
Endukantee the librarian knows:
Where each book is
Who borrowed it
When it should be returned
Which shelf it belongs to
╰┈➤ Similarly a DBMS knows where every piece of data is stored

